{"tool_name":"netmhciipan","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"netmhciipan","home":"http://www.cbs.dtu.dk/services/NetMHCIIpan/","license":"Other","summary":"Predict binding of peptides to MHC class II molecules. The predictions are available for all three human MHC class II isotypes, HLA-DR, HLA-DP and HLA-DQ, as well as mouse molecules.","addition_date":"2015-01-21T13:29:28Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T13:53:55.420485Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Web application"],"version":["3.0","4.2"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:netmhciipan","cost":"Free of charge (with restrictions)","credit":[{"email":"mniel@cbs.dtu.dk","name":"Morten Nielsen","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7885-4311","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"CBS","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"Edita Karosiene","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://www.cbs.dtu.dk/services/NetMHCIIpan/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2044"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}],"note":"Predicts binding of peptides to MHC class II molecules.","operation":[{"term":"Epitope mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0416"},{"term":"Protein binding site prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2575"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Protein features","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1277"},"format":[{"term":"HTML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2331"}]}]}],"maturity":"Emerging","name":"NetMHCIIpan","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"CBS","publication":[{"doi":"10.1007/s00251-013-0720-y","metadata":{"abstract":"Major histocompatibility complex class II (MHCII) molecules play an important role in cell-mediated immunity. They present specific peptides derived from endosomal proteins for recognition by T helper cells. The identification of peptides that bind to MHCII molecules is therefore of great importance for understanding the nature of immune responses and identifying T cell epitopes for the design of new vaccines and immunotherapies. Given the large number of MHC variants, and the costly experimental procedures needed to evaluate individual peptide-MHC interactions, computational predictions have become particularly attractive as first-line methods in epitope discovery. However, only a few so-called pan-specific prediction methods capable of predicting binding to any MHC molecule with known protein sequence are currently available, and all of them are limited to HLA-DR. Here, we present the first pan-specific method capable of predicting peptide binding to any HLA class II molecule with a defined protein sequence. The method employs a strategy common for HLA-DR, HLA-DP and HLA-DQ molecules to define the peptide-binding MHC environment in terms of a pseudo sequence. This strategy allows the inclusion of new molecules even from other species. The method was evaluated in several benchmarks and demonstrates a significant improvement over molecule-specific methods as well as the ability to predict peptide binding of previously uncharacterised MHCII molecules. To the best of our knowledge, the NetMHCIIpan-3.0 method is the first pan-specific predictor covering all HLA class II molecules with known sequences including HLA-DR, HLA-DP, and HLA-DQ. The NetMHCpan-3.0 method is available at http://www.cbs.dtu.dk/services/NetMHCIIpan-3.0. \u00a9 2013 Springer-Verlag Berlin Heidelberg.","authors":[{"name":"Blicher T."},{"name":"Buus S."},{"name":"Karosiene E."},{"name":"Lund O."},{"name":"Nielsen M."},{"name":"Rasmussen M."}],"citationCount":225,"date":"2013-10-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Immunogenetics","title":"NetMHCIIpan-3.0, a common pan-specific MHC class II prediction method including all three human MHC class II isotypes, HLA-DR, HLA-DP and HLA-DQ"},"pmcid":"PMC3809066","pmid":"23900783","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Protein binding sites","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3534"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"NetMHCIIpan","home":"https://bio.tools/netmhciipan","license":"Other","version":["3.0","4.2"],"summary":"Predict binding of peptides to MHC class II molecules. The predictions are available for all three human MHC class II isotypes, HLA-DR, HLA-DP and HLA-DQ, as well as mouse molecules.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:netmhciipan:4.2/cmd/www.cbs.dtu.dk","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"license":{"open_source":false,"osi":false},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":162,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2013"},{"count":4,"year":"2026"},{"count":8,"year":"2014"},{"count":8,"year":"2023"},{"count":9,"year":"2024"},{"count":10,"year":"2021"},{"count":12,"year":"2017"},{"count":13,"year":"2015"},{"count":13,"year":"2019"},{"count":13,"year":"2022"},{"count":13,"year":"2025"},{"count":16,"year":"2018"},{"count":21,"year":"2016"},{"count":21,"year":"2020"}],"doi":"10.1007/s00251-013-0720-y","pmcid":"PMC3809066","pmid":"23900783","ref_count":33,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"1992"},{"count":1,"year":"1995"},{"count":1,"year":"1997"},{"count":1,"year":"2000"},{"count":1,"year":"2003"},{"count":1,"year":"2005"},{"count":1,"year":"2013"},{"count":2,"year":"1999"},{"count":2,"year":"2001"},{"count":2,"year":"2004"},{"count":2,"year":"2011"},{"count":3,"year":"2007"},{"count":3,"year":"2009"},{"count":4,"year":"2008"},{"count":4,"year":"2010"},{"count":4,"year":"2012"}],"title":"NetMHCIIpan-3.0, a common pan-specific MHC class II prediction method including all three human MHC class II isotypes, HLA-DR, HLA-DP and HLA-DQ.","year":2013}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschema